<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Khudabad</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">18th century</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Khudabad is a ruined town near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dadu">Dadu</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sindh">Sindh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a>, founded by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalhora-dynasty">Kalhora dynasty</a> in the early 18th century. It served as the Kalhora capital in the middle of the century, with a large congregational mosque whose remains still stand. The capital later moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyderabad">Hyderabad</a>, founded in 1768, and Khudabad declined.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/khudabad.jpg" alt="Khudabad" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Shakeel Ahmed · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gate_of_Jamia_Mosque_(Khudabad).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
